# ISSUE-0003 minimal nature-trap. target = {2}.
# state 0 action a: stay [0.5,1.0] OR leave to 1 [0.0,0.5]
# Nature (adversarial) can zero the 0->1 edge (lo=0) and keep all mass at 0 forever,
# so the true robust max-reach value V*(0) = 0 (controller can never escape state 0).
# {0} is NOT a support-graph MEC (its action has hi=0.5>0 to state 1), so support-MEC
# collapse leaves it untouched -> interval iteration's upper bound sticks at U(0)=1.
states 3
init 0
label target 2
tran 0 0  0:0.5:1.0 1:0.0:0.5
tran 1 0  2:1:1
tran 2 0  2:1:1
